-- title:
--   Functions integral on both Igusa charts are constants in ℤ_{(ℓ)}
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ be a nonzero natural number and $\ell$ a prime, and let $F =$ `modularFunctionFieldFull N` be the intermediate field of the Laurent series field $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ generated by the $q$-expansions $\mathrm{qExpand}_{\mathbb{Q}}\,d\ j$ for the nonzero divisors $d \mid N$; write $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$ for the subring [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt ℓ`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8) of $\mathbb{Q}$ consisting of the rationals whose denominator is coprime to $\ell$, and let $j \in F$ be the element `jFull N`, i.e. the $q$-expansion $j(q)$ itself. For a subset $S \subseteq F$, `chartAlg N ℓ S` is the $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-subalgebra of $F$ of elements integral over $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}[S]$; the two charts are `chartAlgFin N ℓ` $=$ `chartAlg N ℓ {j}` and `chartAlgInf N ℓ` $=$ `chartAlg N ℓ {j⁻¹}`, the integral closures of $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}[j]$ and of $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}[1/j]$ in $F$. The assertion is: if $x \in F$ is integral over $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}[j]$ and also integral over $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}[1/j]$, then there exists $r \in \mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$ with $x$ equal to the image of $r$ under the structure map $\mathbb{Q} \to F$.
--
--   This is the computation of the global functions on the two-chart integral model of the modular curve over $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$: the two affine Igusa chart rings intersect in the constants $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$, so that the pushout scheme [`ModularCurve.IgusaScheme`](def/ModularCurve_IgusaScheme.html#L255) has $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$ as its ring of global sections. It is used in the proof that the relevant pullback along `igusaTo` composed with a `Spec` map has connected underlying space.
-- source:
